KWin: pointer motion to clients at most once per 750 us (6.7.5 port of patches/kwin/0063, 2026-10-18)

A mouse that reports at 4000-8000 Hz moved the pointer every 125-250 us, and every motion went to the
client under it: its toolkit handled each one (Qt Quick hover delivery, picking) while the screen
shows one position per refresh. The forward input filter now holds a motion that comes less than
KWIN_POINTER_MOTION_INTERVAL_US (default 750; 0 = as before) after the last one sent, and a precise
timer sends the latest; a held motion goes out, with its frame, before any enter, leave, button or
axis event. A 1000 Hz mouse is not affected; warps and locked or confined pointers (games) get every
motion. $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kwin-pointer-motion-interval-us overrides the variable while it exists (read
at most once a second). In 6.7.5 a warp is a motion and a zero relative motion, so it is never held.
Measured on 6.7.91 (findings/qt-pointer-motion-2026-10-18.md): the nested guest's plasmashell at
4000-8000 Hz -51..59 % (its 1000 Hz cost), the guest KWin -10..16 %; clicks after 4000 events/s sweeps
land within 0.1 px; bare metal plasmashell -50..75 %.

